<title>USA: New US CPI-indexed bonds will have 10-yr maturity.</title>
<headline>New US CPI-indexed bonds will have 10-yr maturity.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1996-09-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>A new inflation-linked Treasury bond will have a 10-year maturity linked to the Consumer Price Index, White House officials said.</p>
<p>President Clinton is to announce the issuance of the new bond at a campaign stop in Pittsburgh. The first issue will be a 10-year bond to be sold in January 1997.</p>
<p>&quot;They will be indexed to the CPI,&quot; said a White House official. The bonds are to be issued quarterly after the initial January offering.</p>
</text>
